R-204 batch 2 — accounts in the web UI (web/): sign-in/sign-up, session, workspaces, members, roles, invitations (D-153)
branch: m10/r204-web   base: main 27bfc5a463ea2d4f3075c64d99f7bbb7293a5dab (merge of PR #364, R-204 batch 1)
date: 2026-11-13
scope: web/ only (no server, API or database change). NOT deployed. Uses the /api/v2 routes of batch 1 exactly as documented in API.md.

## 1. What was added
- web/src/session.js — the only place that talks to /api/v2:
  - access token in memory only (never localStorage/sessionStorage, never in a URL, never exposed to components: getSession() returns user + expiry only);
  - page reload restores the session through the HttpOnly refresh cookie (POST /api/v2/auth/refresh), no password;
  - 401 -> exactly one refresh + one retry; concurrent 401s share one refresh (single flight); token refreshed before a call when it expires within 30 s;
    refresh refused or still 401 after refresh -> local session ended (no loop);
  - sign-out: POST /api/v2/auth/logout with the token, local session ends even if the server cannot confirm;
  - OAuth (Google/GitHub) prepared: PKCE S256, verifier kept in sessionStorage for the redirect only and removed when used; return without verifier refused locally;
  - completeFromUrl(): ?code (OAuth), #invite=<token>, provider errors, implicit e-mail-confirmation tokens (that session is ENDED, never adopted); the URL is cleaned every time;
  - pending invitation token kept for this tab only (sessionStorage), current workspace id in localStorage (an id, not a secret);
  - API errors -> Arabic messages keeping the server detail.
- web/src/components/Account.jsx + tab «الحساب» in App.jsx + account-* styles in index.css:
  - sign-in / sign-up; provider buttons only for providers the server enables (/api/v2/auth/config); honest message when accounts are not configured on the server;
  - workspace switcher, create, rename (owner/admin), delete (owner);
  - members: role select only for the owner; remove rules follow the server (owner any non-self, admin members only); «مغادرة» for self, hidden for the only owner (the server refuses it, AG409);
  - invitations: owner may invite admin/member, admin member only; the link is shown ONCE after creation; revoke; pending-invitation banner with accept / ignore;
  - an invitation link opened in an already-open page (hash change, no reload) is picked up too (hashchange listener).

