## 5. Browser check against a REAL local stack (not mocks)
stack: PostgreSQL 18 with docs/sql/v2/001+002, Supabase Auth (GoTrue) v2.197.0 (the binary CI uses), server.app serving web/dist on http://localhost:8765
(the fixture of tests/test_r204_accounts_live.py, unchanged). Sandbox Chrome.
- sign-up owner@demo.test -> «تحقق من بريدك» (confirmation required); sign-in before confirmation -> «البريد لم يُؤكَّد بعد…» (403); confirmed (SQL, local only) -> sign-in OK.
- created workspace «فريق التجربة»; invitation for member@demo.test (role member) -> link shown once; after reload not shown again; pending row with «إلغاء».
- browser storage after sign-in: localStorage = {agos_workspace: <id>} only; sessionStorage = {}; document.cookie = "" (refresh cookie is HttpOnly).
- reload -> session restored without password.
- sign-out -> sign-in form; invitation link opened in the SAME page while signed out -> ignored (defect 1, section 2); full load -> picked up, URL cleaned to "/".
- after fix: same-page hash -> banner shown, URL cleaned; member@demo.test accepted -> «انضممت إلى المساحة بدور عضو»; member view: no role select, no rename/delete,
  no invitation form, «مغادرة» only; members (2) list shows the owner.
- owner view before fix offered «مغادرة» to the only owner (defect 2); plain .btn buttons rendered with the browser default white background and the delete
  button stretched full width -> fixed (btn-ghost, align-self) and re-checked by screenshot.
- sign-out + reload -> sign-in form; GET /api/v2/workspaces without token = 401; POST /api/v2/auth/refresh with the old cookie = 401 (session really ended).

## 5b. Gap found by the existing R-200 gate (tests/test_r200_truth_inventory.py::test_route_parser_on_the_real_repo)
- red: with the new web calls, unmatched_calls(web/src) = 10 calls to /api/v2/* (first: /api/v2/auth/config). Cause: scripts/build_route_inventory.py read only
  `@app.<method>` in server.py + civilization_routes.py, so the 19 /api/v2 routes of batch 1 (APIRouter(prefix="/api/v2") in agos_v2/accounts_api.py) were
  missing from the inventory already on main (len(rows) stayed 31 — that gap was invisible while no web call existed).
- fix: the tool also reads agos_v2/accounts_api.py and applies the APIRouter prefix (`name = APIRouter(prefix=...)`); only decorators of `app` or of a known
  router count; a missing source file stays an error. Test strengthened (not relaxed): 50 rows = 31 + 19, all 19 v2 rows sourced from accounts_api.py,
  login and invitations/accept used by the web UI, and still no web call matching no route.
- after: tests/test_r200_truth_inventory.py 9 passed. The committed R-200 snapshot (REPORT_AR.md, main f1932887) is historical and is not regenerated.

## 5c. Time-fragile test found by the full local suite (batch 1 test, fixed here)
- full suite (local, 744 s): tests/test_r204_accounts_unit.py::test_bad_claims_are_refused[over3-not_yet_valid] and [over4-not_yet_valid] FAILED
  "DID NOT RAISE TokenError"; alone: 39 passed. Cause: the parametrize values {"nbf": int(time.time()) + 600} / {"iat": ...} are computed at COLLECTION;
  the suite reached the test > 600 s later, so "the future" was already past. CI passed only because it reached the test sooner.
- red, reproduced deterministically: plugin /tmp/shiftplug/shift_after_collect.py (collection sees the clock 660 s in the past, tests the real clock):
  =========================== short test summary info ============================
  FAILED tests/test_r204_accounts_unit.py::test_bad_claims_are_refused[over3-not_yet_valid]
  FAILED tests/test_r204_accounts_unit.py::test_bad_claims_are_refused[over4-not_yet_valid]
  ================= 2 failed, 12 passed, 25 deselected in 1.05s ==================
- fix: In(seconds) = time relative to the moment the token is built (claims() resolves it); exp/nbf/iat cases use it. Same plugin after the fix: 39 passed;
  without it: 39 passed. Other time.time() uses in the R-204 tests are inside test bodies (computed at run time).

